| Operational state | Encrypted JSON backup restore drilled in throwaway PostgreSQL; full clean VPS/volume/PITR unverified |

### Architecture and ownership map
```mermaid
flowchart LR
  NAS[NAS devices] --> RAD[RADIUS Auth / Accounting / RadSec]
  RAD --> DB[(PostgreSQL tenant-owned data)]
  WEB[React Admin UI] --> API[Go Admin API / auth / tenancy]
  API --> DB
  POLL[ICMP TCP HTTP SNMP monitor] --> DB
  SYS[UDP syslog ingest] --> DB
  JOB[Scheduler billing / FUP / notifications / retry] --> DB
  JOB --> COA[Durable session action queue -> NAS]
  DB --> NOC[NOC Impact and Customer Timeline endpoints]
  API --> NOC
```
**Module ownership:** `internal/radiusd/` packet pipelines; `internal/adminapi/` operator/tenant APIs; `internal/billing/` financial transitions; `internal/app/` lifecycle, scheduler and migration; `internal/tenancy/` model-level GORM scoping; `internal/networkmonitor/` limited read-only probes; `internal/syslogd/` UDP logs; `internal/sessionqueue/` NAS action retry; `web/src/pages` + `web/src/components` operator interaction. Tenant context and source-based evidence are mandatory across all new read paths.

### Current strengths
- Separation between protocol service, billing, operations and UI; actual tests across major domains.
- Two-branch automation now synchronized at one SHA, releases with SemVer and changelog.
- M18 containment and the completed ten #45–#54 issues produced voucher activation, NOC impact, timeline, safer backup and durable session actions.
- Current docs clearly label unsupported quota/payment-provider endpoints, recovery limitations, and historical operational evidence.
- Feature checklist, AGENT instructions and roadmap explicitly prohibit uncontrolled product expansion.
### Current weaknesses and unknowns
- NAS secret in public model JSON response and missing DTO redaction (verified static security exposure).
- RADIUS accounting ACK is sent before worker-pool acceptance; source demonstrates possible loss on saturation (verified code).
- Syslog IP attribution ambiguous with shared private NAS IP; queue-drop and DB errors not surfaced.
- FUP and billing are business-critical and require load/overlap correctness testing, not just a green unit suite.
- Playwright config points at `web/e2e`, but no `web/e2e` paths in inspected complete Git tree.
- Clean-host VPS upgrade matrix, full-volume restore, off-host backup and PITR not yet demonstrated in documented drills.
- Real NAS compatibility, QoE data quality and operator field feedback remain unknown (not inferred production claims).

